4. CHECK CONSTRAINTS — 43 == 43; 1 differs
================================================================================
  sc.goods_receipt_note status CHECK:
    Dev  allows {In Process, Completed, Partially Completed, Rejected, Closed}            (5 values)
    EF   allows {In Process, Completed, Partially Completed, Rejected, Quality Checked, Closed} (6)
    UAT  == EF (also has 'Quality Checked').
  → Here DEV is the OUTLIER vs UAT/EF (Dev's GRN check predates 'Quality Checked'). EF is the SUPERSET.
  → For stamping: EF's looser check would accept rows Dev's stricter check rejects. Since EF will not
    re-create existing constraints on a stamped DB, Dev keeps its stricter check. CLASSIFY: BLOCKING-LITE
    — a documented intentional widening could make it EXPECTED, but as-is Dev != UAT here and the EF
    model believes 'Quality Checked' is legal while Dev's DB will reject it. Reconcile by altering Dev's
    check to add 'Quality Checked' (forward, non-destructive).
  All other 42 CHECKs match exactly.

