7. AUDIT SCHEMA (AddAuditChangeLog)
================================================================================
  Dev has NO audit schema (confirmed: 0 references in dev.schema.sql). AddAuditChangeLog's Up() is
  fully idempotent raw SQL (CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS audit; CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS
  audit.change_log range-partitioned; existence-guarded grants/trigger).
  → EXPECTED, but a stamping NUANCE: AddAuditChangeLog must be **applied** to Dev (it will create the
    schema), NOT merely stamped-as-applied. If Dev is stamped at BOTH migrations, the audit schema
    will be missing. Recommended: stamp Baseline, then RUN `dotnet ef database update` so
    AddAuditChangeLog actually executes against Dev.

