9. VERDICT
================================================================================
  *** NEEDS RECONCILIATION — but the object that must be reconciled is the EF BASELINE, not Dev. ***

  Dev is internally faithful to UAT (the proven-good shape) on 92 columns, 19 FK rules, generated
  columns, PKs, unique keys, partial indexes, sequences, and 42/43 CHECKs. The current baseline
  `20260603164745_Baseline` has REGRESSED from UAT on the surface listed in §8 (BLOCKING). Stamping
  Dev as-is would make the EF model authoritatively WRONG about Dev: the next model-diff migration EF
  generates would emit ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE timestamptz / SET NOT NULL / TYPE integer, DROP DEFAULT,
  and ALTER FK statements that contradict UAT — risking insert failures (lost auto-numbering),
  data-narrowing on a generated column, and timezone re-interpretation.

  DO NOT stamp Dev against this baseline yet.

  Required fixes BEFORE stamping (fix the MODEL/baseline so EF-built == UAT == Dev), then re-run this
  gate:
    R1. Map the 22 timestamp/date columns to `timestamp without time zone` / `date` (Npgsql:
        .HasColumnType("timestamp without time zone") / "date"), NOT timestamptz. (§2a)
    R2. Make the 49 §2b columns OPTIONAL (.IsRequired(false)) to match UAT nullability. (§2b)
    R3. common.image/video.file_size → int (integer), not long. sc.inventory_stock.qty_available →
        keep generated numeric(18,4) nullable (do not declare integer). (§2c)
    R4. Attach the 7 nextval() defaults via HasDefaultValueSql("nextval('...'::regclass)") (or model
        the columns as DB-generated). (§2d)
    R5. Add HasDefaultValue(0) on the 5 §2e weight/amount/price columns. (§2e)
    R6. Make the 5 §2f columns REQUIRED (sequence, status, work_order_step_id, qty_issued, part_id). (§2f)
    R7. Restore FK delete behaviours to match UAT: SET NULL on the 5 edges EF dropped it from; revert
        common.address.country_id and common.approval.approver_id from CASCADE to SET NULL; drop the
        spurious SET NULL EF added on work_order_task.work_order_step_id. (§3)
    R8. (Dev-side, separate) Widen Dev's sc.goods_receipt_note status CHECK to add 'Quality Checked'
        so Dev == UAT == model. Forward, non-destructive. (§4)
    R9. Stamp policy: after R1–R8 make EF-built==UAT==Dev, stamp Dev at Baseline ONLY, then APPLY
        AddAuditChangeLog (it creates the audit schema Dev lacks). (§7)

  Re-run the build-and-diff in this file after R1–R7; expected result then: 0 BLOCKING column/FK
  deltas → STAMP-SAFE.
